tion of $99K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["CTO Realty Growth, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $781M market cap on $150M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 74% confirm genuine pricing power.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 189% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.8861531026962035},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has perman